  "body": "A tool stores ONE work material's cutting data: a single `material_group`, `rpm` and `feed` (`crates/tools/src/tools.rs:175-179`).\n\n**Effect:** a shop that cuts aluminium, steel, stainless, brass and plastics with the same cutters has to keep one tool library per material (5× the files and tools), or retype speeds per job. The `tool_material` + `flutes` suggestion (`app/src/cutting.rs`) helps interactively, but stored, vetted per-material values can't live on the tool.\n\n**Fix sketch:** an optional per-material table on a tool (material → rpm, feed, and optionally stepdown/stepover), with the operation picking the row for the setup's stock material, and `rpm`/`feed` as the fallback.\n- Save/load: an additive optional key, so old files load unchanged.\n- MCP and UI to edit it.\n\nEffort: high, since feeds reach the posted program.\n\n**Done means:** one tool carries values for several materials; an operation on a stock of material X posts X's row; old files unchanged; pinned.\n",
